## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of cross-store writes with explicit TTLs and cache invalidation. It checks how writes propagate across Redis, MongoDB, Cassandra, and DynamoDB, plus how to keep a hot cache coherent.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-store write paths with idempotence
- TTL-based bucketing in Cassandra
- Cache invalidation and refresh strategies in Redis
- Read path with locality and fallback

## Code Example
```javascript
async function writeMessage(chatId, userId, text, ts){
  await redis.hset(`chat:presence:${userId}`, 'online', 1);
  const msgId = generateId();
  await mongo.messages.insertOne({chat_id: chatId, msg_id: msgId, sender_id: userId, ts, text});
  await cassandra.execute("INSERT INTO messages_by_chat (chat_id, bucket, ts, msg_id) VALUES (?, bucket(?), ?, ?)", [chatId, ts, ts, msgId]);
  await dynamo.archive({chat_id: chatId, msg_id: msgId, ts, text});
  await redis.publish(`chat:updates:${chatId}`, JSON.stringify({msg_id: msgId}));
}
```

